\paragraph{RLVR training dynamics.}
\citet{rlsqueezes2026} show RLVR \emph{compresses} incorrect trajectories while SFT \emph{expands} correct ones; our results qualify this: the asymmetry manifests as a recovery capacity difference, but the expected accuracy gap vanishes when pruning preserves diversity ($|\Delta| \leq 1.8$\,pp; \S\ref{sec:decoupling}).
\citet{mukherjee2025rlsubnetworks} find RL updates only 5--30\% of parameters; we show the pruning criterion shapes which subnetwork remains active, determining RL collapse susceptibility.
